1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,063
Want your Shopee orders in a spreadsheet? Let’s do it with Trako Order Exporter

2
00:00:05,063 --> 00:00:05,740
Here’s how.

3
00:00:06,950 --> 00:00:09,009
First, install Trako in Chrome

4
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:12,442
Sign in to Shopee as usual, then open My Purchases

5
00:00:12,442 --> 00:00:16,286
The Trako panel appears on the page, ready when you are.

6
00:00:17,492 --> 00:00:21,067
Before you start, scroll down to load the orders you want

7
00:00:21,067 --> 00:00:23,701
If Shopee shows a Load More button, use it

8
00:00:23,701 --> 00:00:27,213
Trako scans only the orders already loaded on this page.

9
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:30,657
Ready? Click Export orders to CSV

10
00:00:30,657 --> 00:00:32,664
Trako checks the loaded orders

11
00:00:32,664 --> 00:00:38,082
The export is designed for completed orders, so other order statuses are skipped.

12
00:00:39,283 --> 00:00:43,380
You can follow the progress and estimated time right in the panel

13
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:47,036
Trako may open temporary order tabs while checking details

14
00:00:47,036 --> 00:00:49,179
Need to stop? Click Cancel export.

15
00:00:50,408 --> 00:00:52,829
When the scan finishes, check the result

16
00:00:52,829 --> 00:00:57,246
Skipped products include a reason, like an order that is still To Receive

17
00:00:57,246 --> 00:00:59,062
To try again, click Scan again

18
00:00:59,062 --> 00:01:02,148
Load more orders first if you want to include more.

19
00:01:03,367 --> 00:01:06,496
Next, choose a folder for your CSV and click Save

20
00:01:06,496 --> 00:01:10,711
Give the file a name you’ll recognize, so it’s easy to find later.

21
00:01:11,950 --> 00:01:14,122
Open the CSV in your spreadsheet app

22
00:01:14,122 --> 00:01:17,983
Each product gets its own row, with the details Trako could read

23
00:01:17,983 --> 00:01:20,516
Widen narrow columns if you see hash marks

24
00:01:20,516 --> 00:01:23,774
Some fields can stay blank when they aren’t available.

25
00:01:24,992 --> 00:01:29,280
And that’s it! Load your orders, scan with Trako, and save your CSV

26
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:33,824
Your order data stays in your browser and is not sent to Trako servers.

